e: badge built only for tasks with nested tasks. Test creating a task with no subtasks, ensure no badge; add subtasks, badge appears; remove all subtasks, badge disappears? Also possibly badge count showing wrong number (only top-level or nested descendants?). \"built only for tasks that have nested tasks\" suggests a bug where badge appears with \"0\" for every task. Currently not. Maybe bug when expanding/collapsing? Or when adding first subtask the badge shows 0? Let's test.\n\nLet's start with search because it's easy.\n\nFirst, note the due dates. Today might be Nov 19, 2025? Buy milk due Thursday = Nov 20? Hmm \"Due Thursday\" and next header \"Due Tuesday, November 24\". Wait today's status bar shows 12:24. Let me consider actual dates: Nov 20 2025 is Thursday. Nov 24 is Monday, not Tuesday. Hmm year unknown. Dec 4 Friday, Dec 14 Monday. In 2026: Dec 4 is Friday, Dec 14 is Monday. Nov 24 2026 is Tuesday, Nov 20 2026 is Friday... \"Due Thursday\" maybe Nov 26? But then Nov 24 before Thursday -> ordering weird. Actually in 2026, Nov 24 is Tuesday and Nov 20 Friday. Hmm \"Due Thursday\" could be Nov 19? no, 2026 Nov 19 is Thursday. So today could be Nov 14 (Saturday) with Buy milk due Nov 19 (Thursday), Pack due Nov 24 (Tuesday, 10 days), Pay rent Dec 4 (20 days), Dec 14 (30 days). That fits perfectly! Today = Saturday, November 14, 2026. Buy milk due Thursday Nov 19 (5 days), Pack for trip Nov 24 (10 days), Pay rent Dec 4 (20 days), 30 days = Dec 14. Yes.\n\nSo dates: Buy milk Thu Nov 19; Pack Tue Nov 24; Pay rent Fri Dec 4; Water/Final/Weekly Mon Dec 14; Read docs no date.\n\nNow the task list: header \"Due Monday, December 14\" groups three tasks. Fine.\n\nLet's test the editor by tapping \"Buy milk\". Check fields: title, notes, due date, repeat. Then maybe modify and revert.\n\nBut before mutating, maybe do search tests first (non-destructive). Let me tap Search."}
