{"type": "thinking", "text": "Aha! \"Final dose rescheduled for December 14\". Hmm, that's interesting. Final dose occurs 1 time, due Dec 14. Rescheduled for December 14? That might mean it got rescheduled to the same date? Wait maybe 1 day later should be Dec 15. Snackbar says Dec 14. Possibly due date changed from Dec 14 to Dec 14 but at a different time? The due date only has date no time shown. Hmm.\n\nWait maybe the app rescheduled because \"occurs 1 time\" interprets completing as rescheduling to the next occurrence which doesn't exist? Actually weird. Let's see current list: Final dose still present? It is listed as [20] still with due Dec 14. And snackbar says rescheduled for December 14. So its due date may be unchanged (or changed to different time of day?) but it remains in list. This looks like a bug: a task repeating daily for 1 occurrence only should not be rescheduled at all; completing it should complete it (remove from list). Or maybe the intended behavior: for count=1, complete task and no new occurrence. But the app rescheduled \"for December 14\", i.e., no advance. Hmm.\n\nBut wait — maybe rescheduling to same date is because completion happens and the new occurrence is created on the same date (repeat count 1 means end after 1 occurrence but the engine still generates an occurrence?). Hmm. Let me inspect what changed: open Final dose editor to see repeat settings and due date. Maybe due date became Dec 14 again but recurrence count consumed? Let's check.\n\nActually, importantly, maybe the bug is about the changed \"simpler rule\": it reopens completed repeating tasks by simply adding interval without respecting the repeat count. For Final dose, since repeat interval is daily, the next occurrence should be Dec 15, and the count would be exhausted, so no new task. The app instead rescheduled to Dec 14 (same date) which is nonsensical. But maybe the due date shown is Dec 14 because the new due date is Dec 14 at 11:00? Wait, 1 occurrence daily from due date Dec 14 00:00? Hmm.\n\nLet's check the editor and the actual due date/time. Also check \"Recently modified\"/completed? There's a \"Recently modified\" count 4 in drawer, but maybe not.\n\nLet's undo first to restore, then reopen editor and inspect precisely. Undo [30]."}
