{"type": "thinking", "text": "After completion, editor shows same due date and same repeat config. So the \"reopen\" simply rescheduled to same date (no change) — effectively the task didn't advance at all. Hmm actually maybe the \"rescheduled for December 14\" is because due date was rescheduled from... it may have set due time? The due date row only shows date. What if the next occurrence was Dec 14 at some time (e.g., current time 12:24)? Original due date maybe date-only (00:00). We can tap due date row to see the picker's date/time. But maybe not necessary.\n\nMain point: task should have been completed (removed), not rescheduled. This is likely bug #1.\n\nWait, but maybe Tasks.org's semantics: recurrence count=1 means it occurs once, and upon completion the task is completed and no next occurrence. Yes. The new \"simpler rule\" may be: if repeated, reschedule regardless. The bug manifested as rescheduling to same date. Hmm but why same date? Possibly because the RRULE COUNT=1 means \"reschedule to next occurrence\", and calculation with count 1 returns same due date? Could be a different bug: when repeat count exhausted, the next occurrence calc returns current due date. Either way, wrong.\n\nWe should also test completion of a repeating task with no end (Pay rent, hourly, weekly) works — done. Good.\n\nNow let's consider if \"rescheduled for December 14\" might be due to something else: maybe the repeat setting of Final dose isn't \"daily 1 occurrence\" but \"daily from completion date\"? The editor says \"Repeats daily, occurs 1 time\". It remains on Dec 14. Completion should remove it once count exhausted. Yes bug.\n\nBefore filing, maybe check how other apps handle. I'm confident.\n\nAlso potential bug: completing the parent task \"Pack for trip\" with incomplete subtasks. In Tasks.org, completing parent may complete subtasks too? Let's test later; completion of parent with subtasks could be relevant to repeating engine? Not necessary but list behavior.\n\nNow let's investigate the \"active list filter reapplied whenever editor is opened\" area. What is \"active list filter\"? Could be the search filter. Let's test:\n1. Search \"milk\" -> open Buy milk editor -> save/back -> does list remain filtered? If filter lost, that's a bug. Also maybe edit a task from search result changing something that no longer matches filter: e.g., search \"milk\", edit title to \"Buy milk 2\", save; should disappear from results (filter reapplied). Hmm \"reapplied whenever the editor is opened\" - maybe means when the editor is opened, the list underneath is refreshed according to the active filter. E.g., search \"milk\", complete task? Hmm.\n\nAlternatively the \"active list filter\" could be a saved filter (Filters in drawer). There are no predefined filters. \"Create new filter\" exists. Hard to test creating filter (we can, but maybe heavy).\n\nMaybe it's about the list filter being lost after opening editor from drawer navigation? Let's think of Tasks.org behavior: The task list has a \"filter\" (e.g., My Tasks, Today, Recently modified, tag, search). When you open the task editor, then press Back, the list re-applies filter. That's normal.\n\nThe changed note suggests a regression: \"active list filter is now reapplied whenever the editor is opened.\" Perhaps the bug is that a filter is applied incorrectly on top of search? Hmm.\n\nLet me test the search-filter persistence. Search \"milk\", open task, back. Check search still active with \"milk\". Then maybe edit and save, check results update.\n\nActually before more mutation, let's finish the current undo: Final dose was rescheduled. Should I undo to restore? The task remains but state may be modified (e.g., completed instance counted). To keep preconditions stable, Undo by reopening list and tapping Undo — but the snackbar may be gone since we opened editor. Does opening editor dismiss snackbar? Yes likely. Then undo isn't available. The task remains, possibly with completion history. That's a data change beyond testing. Hmm. We can \"undo\" through app? There may be no. Alternatively, we can set the task back via editor? It already shows same due date/repeat. The only change may be internal completion count. That's acceptable as test mutation? The instructions say do not change data outside testing requires; we did change. We could try undo from task editor? No.\n\nMaybe the snackbar still exists when we go back. Let's check: press BACK to list and see if Undo still available (snackbar usually 5s; it's likely gone now after a few seconds). We'll see.\n\nLet's press BACK."}
