app saved a different task? No, the new task editor had title \"QA badge\" and no subtasks. Hmm.\n\nWait, maybe the Undo of Charge phone completion we did earlier hadn't persisted the Test subtask? Let's trace:\n- We added Test subtask to Pack for trip and saved. Badge 3, row visible.\n- Then various searches.\n- We completed Charge phone -> badge 2, row order changed (completed at bottom).\n- Undo -> badge 3, rows restored (Test subtask at [15]).\n- Then created new task \"QA badge\" -> saved -> badge 2, Test subtask gone.\n\nOdd. Could the new task have been created as a subtask of Pack for trip? No — the fab in main list creates top-level task. Wait, when I tapped fab, was the focus on Pack for trip? No.\n\nAnother possibility: The \"Test subtask\" row is a subtask, and when any task is created/saved, the list rebuilds and the subtask \"Test subtask\" (with trailing newline in title!) fails to render due to the newline? Hmm, but it showed before.\n\nLet me scroll and inspect the whole list. Use swipe down to top? Let's first scroll up (finger up) a bit to see Pack and No due date. Let me observe with a swipe up 0.3."}
