{"type": "thinking", "text": "Confirmed: QA sub3 is top-level (x=540) under No due date, no due date, not a child of Pack. This is bug #2 (or #1 alongside Final dose). Let me now file the reports. But first, let me double-check the \"Final dose\" bug and the exact user-visible text. The snackbar said \"Final dose rescheduled for December 14\". Is the expected behavior definitely \"complete and remove\"? Let me verify from the app's UI: Final dose's repeat row says \"Repeats daily, occurs 1 time\". If a task occurs once, completing it should end the recurrence. In Tasks.org, yes, completing a task with recurrence count 1 marks it done. Let's check the app's online docs? Can't. But logically.\n\nActually, wait: maybe the app's semantics for \"occurs 1 time\" is that it repeats daily once *after each completion*? No, \"occurs 1 time\" means total occurrences = 1. So after completing, no more. The snackbar \"rescheduled for December 14\" (same date) also indicates a broken next-occurrence computation. It stays on the list, so no progress; repeatedly completing it never ends. Definitely a bug.\n\nCould the seeded \"simpler rule\" be: completed repeating tasks are reopened regardless of repeat count; the bug is exactly that tasks with exhausted recurrence are reopened. And Final dose is provided to test that. So yes, report.\n\nNow, before filing, I want to also test the \"editor active list filter\" more concretely and possibly find another seeded bug. Let's inspect the \"Default list\" issue: Maybe it's not a bug; maybe \"My Tasks\" is the default list and \"Default list\" is a local list created by QA setup? Wait, look at the drawer: My Tasks count 11, Default list count 4. The original tasks' editor showed \"Default list\", but they are not in the Default list view. That's a glaring inconsistency! It might be the seeded \"active list filter reapplied whenever editor is opened\" bug: The editor is **assigning** tasks to the wrong list (\"Default list\") because of the active filter, or it is showing the filter's list rather than the task's actual list. Hmm! But wait, all tasks (original) are in My Tasks view; their editor chip says \"Default list\". The Default list view contains only the QA tasks (created in this session) — but those new tasks' editor chip also says \"Default list\". So all tasks claim Default list, yet original tasks don't appear in Default list.\n\nHold on — maybe the original tasks are not in any list (i.e., listId = null / inbox), and the editor chip for \"no list\" displays \"Default list\" (meaning task will be placed in default list if saved?). When you open the editor for a task with no list, the app might assign it to the default list and save that silently? If so, saving Buy milk with no changes might have moved it to the default list! That could be the \"active list filter\" bug: opening the editor reapplies a filter (default list) and thereby changes the task's list to Default list. Hmm!\n\nLet me test this carefully:\n- The original tasks currently appear in My Tasks. Are they in the Default list after we opened/saved some editors? We opened and saved Buy milk (twice: once via Back, once via Save). We opened Pack and saved (with subtasks). We opened Final dose and saved? No, only Back. If opening+saving assigns Default list, Buy milk and Pack should now be in Default list. But Default list showed only QA tasks — no Buy milk, no Pack. So no.\n\nWait, Default list showed only QA sub, QA sub2, QA top, QA top2 (4). Hmm, but *all* subtasks added (QA sub etc.) fell into Default list, while original tasks didn't. That suggests the original tasks are in a different list, and the QA tasks (created during this session) were created in Default list because the new-task editor's list chip \"Default list\" was preselected. So what list are original tasks in? Their editors show \"Default list\" too though... unless the chip is showing the *default* for new tasks, not the current task's list! Maybe the app has a bug where the editor's list chip always displays \"Default list\" (the app's default) regardless of the task's actual list. Then opening and saving the editor without changing the list would move the task to Default list? But Buy milk wasn't moved (still not in Default list). Unless my Save of Buy milk didn't actually save because no changes (app detects no changes and doesn't update). Hmm.\n\nLet's test: Open Buy milk, tap the list chip to see which list is selected in the list picker. If the picker shows \"My Tasks\" (or another list) selected, then the chip text is wrong. Let's do that. Scroll to top, open Buy milk, tap list chip.\n\nThis is worth investigating because the \"Task editor screen: active list filter is now reapplied whenever the editor is opened\" change is in scope. Maybe the bug: opening the editor shows the active list filter instead of the task's actual list, and saving could move the task to the filtered list. Hmm.\n\nLet's inspect. Scroll down 0.5 to top."}
