{"type": "thinking", "text": "Confirmed! With an empty search query and keyboard hidden, pressing Back exits the app to the launcher instead of returning to the task list. This is exactly in the changed area (\"Task list search: the system Back gesture during search is now handled by the main screen\"). Expected: Back should close search and show the task list. Observed: app closes to home screen. This is a solid bug to report.\n\nBut wait: is it specific to empty query? With \"milk\" it exited search. Let me verify the \"milk\" case again to characterize:\n- Reopen app (My Tasks).\n- Search, type \"milk\", hide keyboard, press BACK -> should return to list (we saw earlier).\nThen maybe also test with empty query once more to confirm (reproduce twice). We just reproduced once. The instructions say reproduce a problem once before reporting (i.e., verify once). We did reproduce twice actually (the earlier Save scenario and now). Good.\n\nBut I should be precise: The first time (Save scenario) the query was empty too. So the condition is empty query. Let's confirm with a fresh non-empty query quickly to be sure the bug is specific to empty query and not random. Reopen app, search, type \"milk\", BACK (hide keyboard), BACK -> should show main list. Then search empty, BACK twice -> launcher. That gives a clean contrast.\n\nLet's do it. Open app."}
