{"type": "thinking", "text": "After completion, the task still shows Tomorrow (Nov 15) and repeats daily, occurs 1 time. So the app reopened/rescheduled to the same date, not completed. This is clearly wrong: a 1-occurrence task cannot be completed.\n\nWait, maybe the task is due tomorrow and the completion \"rescheduled for tomorrow\" because when completing a task due in the future, Tasks.org might not advance the due date? Hmm, in Tasks.org, completing a repeating task that is due tomorrow should advance to the next occurrence based on its due date (Nov 16) or completion date (Nov 15). It shouldn't keep it tomorrow. But the app might treat completing a future task differently: maybe it \"reschedules for tomorrow\" because complete on a future-dated task just marks it done and creates a new occurrence at... no.\n\nCould it be that the app doesn't allow completing a task due in the future via the checkbox? But the snackbar says rescheduled. Hmm.\n\nActually, maybe the bug is that the app **didn't advance** because the recurrence count is 1 and the \"simpler rule\" sets the next due date to the current due date when no next occurrence exists. So yes.\n\nAnyway, the developer couldn't reproduce the Final dose steps. Maybe they tested with a fresh task and saw the same bug but didn't recognize it? Or maybe their build differs? Unlikely. Let's file a new report with the clean steps and mention both. The previous report is not confirmed; a new one may be accepted.\n\nBefore filing, maybe test a **control**: create a task due tomorrow repeating daily \"Never\" (infinite) and complete it, to see it advance to Nov 16. If the control advances but 1-occurrence stays, the bug is specific to count=1. That would strengthen the report. But creating another task detaches QA sub4 (already detached) — fine. However, more test data to clean up. The control is valuable to show expected behavior.\n\nLet's do the control:\n- Close QA repeat once editor (BACK).\n- Create \"QA repeat infinite\" due tomorrow, repeat daily, Ends Never, save.\n- Complete; expect next occurrence Nov 16 (or in 1 day). Observe snackbar \"rescheduled for November 16\".\n- Then delete both QA repeat tasks later.\n\nBut careful: creating QA repeat infinite will detach any newly added subtask; QA sub4 already detached. Fine.\n\nActually, the developer's response \"could not reproduce\" might mean the bug isn't real and the app's behavior is by design. A control helps me decide. Let's do it.\n\nClose editor (BACK). Then FAB, create task. But the current list is scrolled to top with QA repeat once at top. Let's press BACK to close editor."}
