{"type": "thinking", "text": "Clean fresh repro: \"QA repeat once rescheduled for tomorrow\" and the row remains. This is solid.\n\nNote: \"QA repeat once\" was created with due tomorrow (Nov 15), repeat daily, occurs 1 time. Completing it shows rescheduled for tomorrow, no advance. Contrast: \"QA repeat infinite\" (daily, never ends) advanced to Monday Nov 16 correctly.\n\nLet's file a new report with these clean steps, using element_ref 34 (snackbar) and quote \"QA repeat once rescheduled for tomorrow\". The report should clarify this is the same issue as Final dose: 1-occurrence repeat not completing. The developer might then reproduce.\n\nWe need to be careful: the previous report claimed Final dose and was rejected. Maybe filing the same bug again is okay with better steps. Let me phrase it as a new finding with the fresh task. The screen \"My Tasks\".\n\nSteps:\n1. Tap FAB, enter \"QA repeat once\".\n2. Tap due date -> Tomorrow -> OK.\n3. Tap \"Does not repeat\" -> Every day -> tap \"Repeats daily\" row -> Custom… -> select \"After\" 1 occurrence -> OK (and ensure \"Repeats from due date\").\n4. Save. Task appears due Tomorrow with \"Repeats daily, occurs 1 time\".\n5. Tap its complete checkbox.\n6. Observed: snackbar \"QA repeat once rescheduled for tomorrow\" and the task stays in the list with the same due date; reopening shows same repeat setting. Expected: since the recurrence has only 1 occurrence, completing it should mark it complete and remove it from the active list (no next occurrence).\n\nAlso mention control: an otherwise identical daily task with Ends Never advances to Monday November 16, so only the 1-occurrence case fails.\n\nLet's file."}
