{"type": "thinking", "text": "Restored badge 2 and both subtasks intact. Good.\n\nNow the \"0\" badge: it's an interesting edge case. Should we report? Let's see the changed note once more: \"Subtask badges on task rows: the badge is now built only for tasks that have nested tasks.\" Since Pack does have nested tasks (2), a badge is built; the count of *remaining* nested tasks is 0. If the intended app behavior is \"badge appears only when there are nested tasks\" and shows count of *incomplete* nested tasks, then 0 is the correct count for all-completed. The note doesn't say the badge should be hidden at 0. So showing 0 may be intended by the change. I won't report it unless the developer confirms. Hmm.\n\nBut maybe the actual seeded bug is that tasks with **no subtasks** still show a badge \"0\" — but ours don't. Since the fix works for the precondition data, maybe the badge area has no bug (the note is just context). Similarly, the editor note may just be context.\n\nWait — maybe the seeded bugs are intentionally introduced and the \"changed\" notes describe the intended behavior, with one or more bugs. Our job is to find bugs in the areas. The search Back bug and the repeat 1-occurrence bug are confirmed. There may be an editor bug and a badge bug. Let's explore more.\n\nMaybe the badge bug is that the count is wrong for **nested subtasks** (sub-subtasks). Let's test: Add a subtask to Charge phone (a nested child). Then check Pack's badge: should it count 3 (all descendants) or 2 (direct children only)? The note \"nested tasks\" might imply all descendants. Hmm. In Tasks.org, the badge likely counts **direct** incomplete subtasks. Let's see what the app shows and whether it seems wrong.\n\nAdd a subtask \"QA nested\" to Charge phone:\n- Open Charge phone editor (tap row).\n- Add subtask \"QA nested\", save.\n- Check Pack badge: if it becomes 3, it counts all descendants; if 2, direct only. Which is correct? Not clear. The term \"nested tasks\" in Tasks.org usually refers to subtasks at any depth; the badge may aggregate. Hmm.\n\nThis is risky. Let's skip unless we observe something clearly wrong.\n\nEditor testing:\n- Rotate while editing, ensure fields kept. Let's test with a precondition task without mutating: open Buy milk, rotate to landscape, check title/notes/due date still there; rotate back; press Back to discard. Good.\n- Empty title: Open FAB, leave title empty, tap Save. What happens? It may save an empty task \"Task name\"? That would be a bug. Let's test carefully; if it creates an empty task, delete it. But our app's title field hint is \"Task name\"; if empty and Save tapped, expected behavior: task should not be saved (or title required). Let's test.\n- Cancel/Back discards: change title then Back, verify original. Could test on Buy milk with a temporary change.\n- Due date/repeat display consistency: open Pay rent, check repeat \"monthly\"; open Water plants, check \"hourly\"; Weekly review \"every 2 weeks\"; Final dose \"daily, occurs 1 time\". We already verified Final dose; let's verify the others' editors to ensure the list/precondition matches (consistency). This could reveal a bug if e.g., Pay rent's repeat is wrong. Let's do that as part of repeating area. We saw list icons; open each.\n\nLet's first test the editor rotation and empty title, as they're quick.\n\nRotate test with Buy milk:\nTap Buy milk [row 7? current observation [7] is Charge phone; Buy milk is above, off-screen? Current list has Due Tuesday at y=245, Buy milk above (Due Thursday) off-screen. Scroll down 0.4 to top."}
